Z||000000||summerjim||10-14-2001||01:40 PM||||Fiero Store has Earl's SS brake lines for $99. (is there another source for these?)<P>CarParts.com has Goodridge G-Stop SS brake lines for $139.<P>Anyone have any experience with either? Is there anotoher set of SS brake lines for the Fiero that are better?<P>thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Banzai||10-14-2001||01:49 PM||||I've got a set of Earls sitting on the shelf for my 84'.  They look to be good quality. Can't help with a installed opinion as I'm still hooking up the engine and driveline.(just put it back in Fri.)  They should definately improve feel though.  I had a set of Goodridge Kevlar lines on my 97 TL1000s and they were kick ass. Blue lines with red anondized fittings.<P>Banzai !!!!!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000002||2birds||10-14-2001||06:58 PM||||I put Goodridge's (from the Fiero Store) on my Fiero back in '95.  Didn't change the brake feel a bit, IMHO, but at $80 for a set of four, it was cheaper than new OEM style lines, even the parts store brands.  Haven't had a problem with them at all.  <BR>Try Summit for the Earl's lines.||||reg||1
